    "title": "Actor Bill Murray at UConn's NCAA Tournament games",
    "text": "Legendary actor and comedian Bill Murray is in attendance for the UConn men's basketball team's Round of 32 matchup with UCLA in the NCAA Tournament Sunday in Philadelphia. Murray was seated a couple rows behind the UConn bench, where his son Luke serves as an assistant coach under Dan Hurley. He also attended the Huskies' opening round victory over Furman from Xfinity Mobile Arena. The 75-year-old actor got his start on Saturday Night Live in the late 1970s and ultimately won two Primetime Emmy Awards and a Golden Globe across his successful entertainment career. Murray famously starred in \"Caddyshack\" and the \"Ghostbusters\" series and frequently collaborates with famed director Wes Anderson. Luke was raised in Palisades, N.Y. and has maintained deep ties to the Nutmeg State beyond his current stint at UConn. He was a two-sport athlete at St. Luke's School in New Canaan and enrolled at Fairfield University while he coached several AAU programs. His first collegiate coaching gig was offered by current Huskies general manager Tom Moore at Quinnipiac, where Murray served as the Bobcats' Director of Basketball Operations. With Hurley hiring Luke to his staff in 2021, Murray became a regular presence at UConn basketball games. Luke has recently been listed as a leading contender for the Boston College head coaching position",
